# Waymark — Launch Checklist

**Author:** Oyugi Mourice · **Last updated:** 2026-10-07

Everything below needs *your accounts or a decision*, so it could not be completed or verified during development.
Work top to bottom; each item says how to know it is done.

## A. Blockers

- [ ] **Code provenance and licence.** The server integration originates from Sahil David's `aurora-app` repository, whose
  commits contain no `LICENSE` file; this repository's `LICENSE` is an MIT licence in your name. Without an explicit
  licence from the original author the default is "all rights reserved". Get written permission (or a licence) from him,
  keep attribution, and resolve this before any public release or commercial use. *Done when:* permission is recorded
  and attribution is in the repository.
- [ ] **Legal review of `/privacy` and `/terms`.** They were written from what the code does and are not legal advice.
  Confirm each statement, especially: the provider list (Meta, Twilio, Trigger.dev, Anthropic, AWS), retention at the
  agent and providers, and governing law (intentionally omitted from the Terms). Check whether you must register with
  Kenya's Office of the Data Protection Commissioner. *Done when:* a qualified reviewer has signed off.
- [ ] **`WAYMARK_CONTACT_EMAIL`** is a mailbox you monitor (the build requires it).
- [ ] **Production WhatsApp sender** approved by Meta (business verification, display name). The Twilio sandbox must not
  be advertised.

## B. Verify on real infrastructure

- [ ] `npm run smoke -- https://<domain>` passes (25 checks locally, 26 over HTTPS).
- [ ] Send a real WhatsApp text, link and photo; each gets a reply.
- [ ] Response headers on `/` and `/privacy` include the CSP (`script-src 'none'`) and HSTS **on the live site**. If the
  CDN serves the prerendered HTML without them, `customHttp.yml` is not being applied — check the Amplify headers page.
- [ ] A second request to `/` shows CDN caching (`x-cache: Hit` or `age` header) — if not, pages are rendered by the
  compute on every view; acceptable, but cost and latency are worse.
- [ ] Trigger.dev idempotency: send the same message twice (replay the signed webhook) and confirm one run.
- [ ] Break the agent on purpose (stop the task): the user receives the "please send it again" message.
- [ ] A message sent > 24 h after the last user message makes `notify` return 422 with `twilioCode: 63016`.

## C. Operations

- [ ] Uptime check on `/api/ready`; error-log alarm; Twilio alerts (RUNBOOK §5).
- [ ] **Spend caps** on the AI provider and Twilio (this is the main mitigation for residual risk R1).
- [ ] CloudWatch log retention set (e.g. 30 days).
- [ ] Trigger.dev and Twilio retention reviewed (R5).
- [ ] GitHub: branch protection on `main` requiring CI, secret scanning + push protection, Dependabot alerts on.
- [ ] Restrict who can read Amplify build artifacts/logs (secrets are baked into them).
- [ ] Calendar reminder for **2026-12-01**: audit exceptions expire.

## D. SEO and answer-engine visibility (after the site is live)

- [ ] `PUBLIC_URL` is the final canonical domain (one domain; redirect www/non-www and http→https).
- [ ] Verify the domain in Google Search Console and Bing Webmaster Tools; submit `/sitemap.xml`.
- [ ] Run Google's Rich Results Test and the Schema.org validator on `/`.
- [ ] Run Lighthouse (mobile) on `/`; run an automated accessibility check (axe). Neither was possible offline.
- [ ] Preview the share card (`/og.png`) in WhatsApp, X/Twitter and LinkedIn.
- [ ] Decide your policy toward AI crawlers (currently all allowed) — `robots.txt` is generated in `server/lib/seo.ts`.

## E. Repository hygiene

- [ ] Remove the committed build output from git: `git rm -r --cached node_modules .output .nuxt` and commit. To also
  drop it from history (the repository is ~50 MB because of it), use `git filter-repo --invert-paths --path node_modules
  --path .output --path .nuxt` — this preserves authorship and the rest of history.
- [ ] Move `docs/mine.md` (a personal, fork-migration guide) out of the public repository.
- [ ] Agent repository: adopt `server/lib/contracts.ts`, the new `notify` status semantics (ARCHITECTURE §5.2), and send
  the user an apology when the agent itself fails.
